Chapter: MathCordicQuadrants
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Math chapter Cordic

 Fixed point at scale 1000, and angles are milliradians. The reference
 figures: sin 0.5 = 0.479, sin 1 = 0.841, sin 2 = 0.909, sin(pi) = 0,
 sin(3pi/2) = -1, cos(pi) = -1, cos(pi/2) = 0.

 CORDIC converges only while the target can be retired by the angle table,
 which sums to 1735 milliradians, so every argument above that is the
 question and every argument below it is a control. cordic-normalize admits
 the whole turn, so before the quadrant fold the three quarters of the
 circle above 1.735 rad all answered one saturated constant: sin(pi) read
 986 rather than 0 and cos(pi) read -168 rather than -1000.

 The residual 3 in every extreme (997 rather than 1000) is the gain
 constant 607 approximating 1/1.6468, and it is present at cos 0 too, so
 it is not the quadrant fold and no row here should be read as measuring
 it.

Section: Body

  s : Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  s (a) (got) (want) = "  sin " & show a & " = " & show got & "  true " & want

  c : Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  c (a) (got) (want) = "  cos " & show a & " = " & show got & "  true " & want

 A point on the unit circle satisfies sin^2 + cos^2 = 1 whatever the
 quadrant, so this is one assertion the saturated version could not have
 passed anywhere above 1735 and it needs no per-angle reference value. It
 is blind to sign, though: sabotaging the third quadrant's sin negation
 left this count at 13 of 13 and moved only the two counts below, which is
 why both kinds of row are here.

  pythag : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pythag (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else let a = i * 500
    in let sn = cordic-sin a
    in let cs = cordic-cos a
    in let m = sn * sn + cs * cs
    in pythag (i + 1) n (if m > 985000 then if m < 1015000 then acc + 1 else acc else acc)

 sin is non-negative on the first half turn and non-positive on the second.
 The saturated version answered 986 for every angle above 1735, so it
 failed the second half at every point.

  upper : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  upper (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else upper (i + 1) n (if cordic-sin (i * 300) >= 0 then acc + 1 else acc)

  lower : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  lower (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i > n then acc
    else lower (i + 1) n (if cordic-sin (3142 + i * 300) <= 0 then acc + 1 else acc)

Section: Report

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "Below 1735 the rotation always converged, so these are controls"
    print-line-uni "and the quadrant fold must not move any of them:"
    print-line-uni (s 0 (cordic-sin 0) "0")
    print-line-uni (s 500 (cordic-sin 500) "479")
    print-line-uni (s 1000 (cordic-sin 1000) "841")
    print-line-uni (s 1500 (cordic-sin 1500) "997")
    print-line-uni (c 0 (cordic-cos 0) "1000, and 997 is the gain constant, not the fold")
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "Second quadrant, where the saturation began:"
    print-line-uni (s 2000 (cordic-sin 2000) "909")
    print-line-uni (s 2500 (cordic-sin 2500) "599")
    print-line-uni (s 3141 (cordic-sin 3141) "0")
    print-line-uni (c 1571 (cordic-cos 1571) "0")
    print-line-uni (c 2000 (cordic-cos 2000) "-416")
    print-line-uni (c 3141 (cordic-cos 3141) "-1000")
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "Third and fourth quadrants, where sin must go negative and the"
    print-line-uni "saturated version answered a positive 986 throughout:"
    print-line-uni (s 3500 (cordic-sin 3500) "-351")
    print-line-uni (s 4712 (cordic-sin 4712) "-1000")
    print-line-uni (s 5500 (cordic-sin 5500) "-706")
    print-line-uni (c 4712 (cordic-cos 4712) "0")
    print-line-uni (c 6000 (cordic-cos 6000) "960")
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "Angles outside one turn, which cordic-normalize folds first:"
    print-line-uni (s 7854 (cordic-sin 7854) "1000, being 6283 + 1571")
    print-line-uni (s (0 - 1571) (cordic-sin (0 - 1571)) "-1000")
    print-line-uni ""
    print-line-uni "Counted rather than eyeballed, over the whole turn:"
    print-line-uni ("  sin^2 + cos^2 within 1.5 pct of 1, angles 0..6000: " & show (pythag 0 12 0) & " of 13")
    print-line-uni ("  sin non-negative over 0..3000:                     " & show (upper 0 10 0) & " of 11")
    print-line-uni ("  sin non-positive over pi..pi+3000:                 " & show (lower 0 10 0) & " of 11")
  end

